WHERE THE GAIN CAN COME FROM, and it is a THEOREM about this family, not a hope:
  deg = a + t, so deg-1 >= 2+k with a <= 1+k forces t >= 2.  On a TRIANGLE-FREE
  vertex t = 0 and the degree half can NEVER win.  Every PG(2,q) incidence graph
  is bipartite, so on those hosts the sharpening is VACUOUS BY CONSTRUCTION.

